    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. All `data_samples()` entries are on one long line — impossible to scan\n2. Many unused data-provider methods copied from the full test class, cluttering the file\n3. Many unused imports\n\nI'll produce a clean version: format the data table one-row-per-line, remove the dead helper methods, and strip unused imports.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes the 7 unused data-provider methods, strips all unused imports, and reformats `data_samples()` so each Julian→ISO mapping appears on its own line with inline comments explaining the calendar offset logic (2-day initial gap, growing by 1 each century that Julian has a leap day but ISO does not)."
    }
